WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:06.080
Henry Cavill had to choose between a super-powerful
metahuman who fights for justice and one that

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:07.150
fights for coin.

00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:11.230
Now, fans have opinions…and conspiracies
about the choice.

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:16.170
Arguably Henry Cavill's two most iconic roles
— Superman from the DC Universe, and Geralt

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:20.738
of Rivia from "The Witcher" — have simultaneously
found their way back into the social spotlight,

00:00:20.738 --> 00:00:22.387
for very different reasons.

00:00:22.387 --> 00:00:26.099
In the weeks leading up to the release of
"Black Adam," Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson's

00:00:26.099 --> 00:00:31.470
antihero passion project, it was revealed,
by The Rock himself that Superman would make

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:32.840
a guest appearance.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:37.650
As the role had been absent from a slew of
recent DC projects, and because Cavill remained

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:42.210
silent about his status as a member of the
DCEU, the general population assumed that

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:43.690
he was done with DC.

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:48.570
Now, however, it's been confirmed by Cavill
himself on Instagram that he will be returning

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:52.370
to the DC Universe for more Superman-centric
content.

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:56.680
Almost immediately after that news dropped,
it was revealed that Netflix had hired Liam

00:00:56.680 --> 00:01:00.269
Hemsworth to take over the role of Geralt
of Rivia for "The Witcher," starting with

00:01:00.269 --> 00:01:03.010
the newly confirmed fourth season.

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:06.920
Because of the timing, these two pieces of
information feel connected, as if Warner Bros.

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:11.721
would require all of Cavill's time moving
forward and he had to choose between the two roles.

00:01:11.721 --> 00:01:16.400
That feels logical, but there's another potential
theory behind Cavill's departure, and it looks

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:17.810
to carry some weight.

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:21.530
Fans took to Twitter to share their view on
the situation, as the idea of Henry Cavill

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:25.930
leaving "The Witcher" just to give DC his
entire focus didn't align with his previous

00:01:25.930 --> 00:01:27.320
statements on the subject.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:31.930
For context, in a 2021 interview with "The
Hollywood Reporter," Cavill promised his ongoing

00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:36.743
commitment to the series, provided that the
content remained faithful to the source material.

00:01:36.743 --> 00:01:38.263
Specifically, the outlet wrote,

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:42.040
"The actor remains committed to supporting
Hissrich's vision to keep 'The Witcher' going

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:44.490
for at least seven seasons.

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:46.079
'Absolutely,' Cavill says.

00:01:46.079 --> 00:01:51.690
'As long as we can keep telling great stories
which honor [author Andrzej] Sapkowski's work.'"

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:53.750
With that in mind, one Twitter user tweeted,

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:58.509
"I like how everyone thinks Henry Cavill left
because [the] Superman role paid more.

00:01:58.509 --> 00:02:02.280
But there's info out there confirming that
a lot of people working on The Witcher hated

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:04.360
the source material and the games.

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:07.950
Henry probably didn't want to continue his
contract and work with them."

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:11.849
That information can be found in articles
where it's revealed that Beau DeMayo, a previous

00:02:11.849 --> 00:02:17.040
producer for "The Witcher," claimed the writers
for the Netflix series actively despised both

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:20.310
Andrzej Sapkowski's books and CD Projekt Red's
games.

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:24.310
If this were to be proven true, then it would
explain why Cavill continued to do interviews,

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:29.120
where he suggests he would love for subsequent
seasons to stay loyal to the books.

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:33.420
This could mean that Cavill would have left
"The Witcher" with or without the safety net

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:35.730
of more DC projects coming down the pipeline.

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:37.670
"Evil is evil, Stregabor.

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:44.000
Lesser, greater, middling, it's all the same."

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:48.750
While it has yet to be officially confirmed
if the writers chose to scorn the source material,

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.430
more and more fans are latching onto the narrative.

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:52.430
One tweet said,

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:56.400
"I'm upset that Henry Cavill is leaving The
Witcher, but I'm even more upset at the audacity

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:01.170
of the Netflix writers in thinking they can
do better than Sapkowski's novels (especially

00:03:01.170 --> 00:03:04.480
after season 2 proved that they, in fact,
cannot)."

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:06.159
While another tweet declared,

00:03:06.159 --> 00:03:11.019
" ... this show is done; season 2 was pretty
bad so makes sense that Henry Cavill left

00:03:11.019 --> 00:03:14.170
... he said he wanted Netflix to be true to
the source material."

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:18.750
No one seems to harbor animosity towards Liam
Hemsworth for joining the cast, but most fans

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:21.700
have stated that they can't even fathom another
actor in the role.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:25.940
Polite indifference to Hemsworth's resume
boost doesn't necessarily equate to viewers

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:27.150
for Netflix.

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:31.700
If social media is any indicator of the future
of the series, "The Witcher" is likely to

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:35.640
see a significant drop in streams from the
third season to the fourth.

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:40.489
In fairness to all involved, the future of
the DC Universe is still on shaky ground,

00:03:40.489 --> 00:03:42.169
too, but that's another story.

